  "question": {
    "text": "If, for a positive integer&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>, the quadratic equation,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>..</mo><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;<br /><br />has two consecutive integral solutions, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to:"
  },
